                        "form": "бато́нах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "82aced19-e35f-34d5-a716-aa28f3c5cd3a",
                        "entry_id": "60fd884e-2a5e-3e37-bffa-fda07d30dfd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "хлебобулочное изделие продолговатой формы"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "befabd82-a7ee-46c2-b0e3-f6a0ee7083ae",
                                "sense_id": "82aced19-e35f-34d5-a716-aa28f3c5cd3a",
                                "text": "Один солдат, вывернув из тряпки огромный батон (витой хлеб пшеничный), разломил его широким разломом и начал есть, даже не понюхав."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2345f83c-bfd3-3c9a-96b8-403a63d37841",
                        "entry_id": "60fd884e-2a5e-3e37-bffa-fda07d30dfd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "колбасное изделие продолговатой формы"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4512ec1-b2a5-4d1e-bd2b-7f5e01525c8f",
                                "sense_id": "2345f83c-bfd3-3c9a-96b8-403a63d37841",
                                "text": "Не колесо, а именно батон толстой варёной колбасы, похожий на дирижабль."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "314a5905-7a9a-456c-9ab1-7a60d4f152b1",
                                "sense_id": "2345f83c-bfd3-3c9a-96b8-403a63d37841",
                                "text": "И сразу из-под прилавка, будто сам по себе, вынырнул батон серой какой-то, безымянной колбасы, бросился с кирпичным стуком на чашу весов, поколебал размашисто стрелку и упаковался в позавчерашнюю «Вечернюю Уфу»."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3967c89b-7bc9-3e82-94a7-4da2ef9a32e0",
                        "entry_id": "60fd884e-2a5e-3e37-bffa-fda07d30dfd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "микроавтобус марки УАЗ"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "29901d48-cda1-4efd-8b5f-256831f6c817",
                                "sense_id": "3967c89b-7bc9-3e82-94a7-4da2ef9a32e0",
                                "text": "С грехом пополам «батон» вытащили, использовав малопригодную в таких случаях короткую сцепку."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b215ff1-2c42-423a-98ec-dc9c70b7ad15",
                                "sense_id": "3967c89b-7bc9-3e82-94a7-4da2ef9a32e0",
                                "text": "Все садятся в салон, и вскоре милицейский батон трогает с места."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "31705b98-7db1-44da-853b-8fa27348c95b",
                        "source_entry_id": "60fd884e-2a5e-3e37-bffa-fda07d30dfd4",
                        "target_lang_word": "loaf",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loaf",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eca4dc2f-bc7a-3390-bf27-08675b8ebc5c",
                                        "entry_id": "6603b455-93f9-3e6b-abcb-15a1236ac421",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A block of bread after baking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea76d4b4-ac8a-4d79-8a90-6000ce53bc18",
                                                "sense_id": "eca4dc2f-bc7a-3390-bf27-08675b8ebc5c",
                                                "text": "Philander went into the next room[…]and came back with a salt mackerel that dripped brine like a rainstorm. Then he put the coffee pot on the stove and rummaged out a loaf of dry bread and some hardtack."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "310c8007-f929-35a4-8568-d3f59b7764b9",
                                        "entry_id": "6603b455-93f9-3e6b-abcb-15a1236ac421",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any solid block of food, such as meat or sugar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fbe7634-7a44-4537-a390-3556b526f1f5",
                                                "sense_id": "310c8007-f929-35a4-8568-d3f59b7764b9",
                                                "text": "sugar-loaf"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52cd4e1c-4c8b-34f7-b18d-8eb24986e064",
                                        "entry_id": "6603b455-93f9-3e6b-abcb-15a1236ac421",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of loaf of bread: the brain or the head."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Cockney",
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef1aff17-a927-4e10-acb3-c75b6a288e15",
                                                "sense_id": "52cd4e1c-4c8b-34f7-b18d-8eb24986e064",
                                                "text": "use one's loaf"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95f0842f-4103-4c72-93d7-bb37b1cd990e",
                                                "sense_id": "52cd4e1c-4c8b-34f7-b18d-8eb24986e064",
                                                "text": "It is frequently said of Bertram Wooster that he is a man who can think on his feet, and if the necessity arises he can also use his loaf when on all fours. [...] “Why didn't the idiot tell her not to open it?” “It was his first move. ‘I've found a letter from you here, precious,’ she said. ‘On no account open it, angel,’ he said. So of course she opened it.” She pursed the lips, nodded the loaf, and ate a moody piece of crumpet. “So that's why he's been going about looking like a dead fish.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c423e082-fc65-3a45-8120-19862a3b857a",
                                        "entry_id": "6603b455-93f9-3e6b-abcb-15a1236ac421",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A solid block of soap, from which standard bar soap is cut."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a072c10-7326-3e85-b744-0cc9c0b32302",
                                        "entry_id": "6603b455-93f9-3e6b-abcb-15a1236ac421",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A particular still life configuration with seven living cells."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d55d5ea1-e55c-4a51-9341-db42005d6ab9",
                                                "sense_id": "6a072c10-7326-3e85-b744-0cc9c0b32302",
                                                "text": "It runs for 17331 generations before stabilizing as 136 blinkers, 109 blocks, 65 beehives, 18 loaves, 18 boats, 7 ships, 4 tubs, 3 ponds, 2 toads, and 40 gliders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78a51af5-9c36-4754-b050-4ce643eac3df",
                                                "sense_id": "6a072c10-7326-3e85-b744-0cc9c0b32302",
                                                "text": "Running a LWSS into it can produce various debris. One of these reactions produces a loaf. When the loaf is properly hit with other LWSSs, it can be pulled backwards."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36c3b88b-ddfe-4929-8fdb-6df598fb51a4",
                                                "sense_id": "6a072c10-7326-3e85-b744-0cc9c0b32302",
                                                "text": "I am looking for the smallest ancestor of the following four loaf pattern in Conway's Game of Life:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f7fb2194-b156-3ef8-a41d-98e63dc8cc15",
                                        "entry_id": "6603b455-93f9-3e6b-abcb-15a1236ac421",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A catloaf."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
